<idea-plugin>
    <id>io.github.saigyo.aslan</id>
    <name>Aslan ASL Editor</name>
    <vendor email="aslan@kaixo.de" url="https://github.com/saigyo/aslan">saigyo</vendor>

    <description><![CDATA[
        <p>Edit and visualize AWS Step Functions state machines written in Amazon States Language (ASL), in YAML and JSON: completion, checks, JSONata, variables, a live diagram and links from comments to code.</p>
        <p><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/saigyo/aslan/main/docs/images/diagram.png" width="700" alt="A definition in the editor beside its diagram, with the selected state's details below"></p>
        <p><b>Editing</b></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Completion of field names, state types, values, error names and state names; a new state gets the fields its type needs</li>
            <li>Checks as AWS applies them at deployment, each an inspection that can be switched off</li>
            <li>Quick documentation for fields, state types and values, with links to the AWS documentation</li>
            <li>Go to, find and rename states, and a structure view of the states</li>
        </ul>
        <p><b>JSONata</b></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Highlighting and syntax checks of <code>{% … %}</code> expressions, exactly as Step Functions parses them</li>
            <li>Completion, quick documentation and parameter hints for functions, <code>$states</code> and local variables</li>
            <li>Go to declaration, find usages and rename for local variables</li>
        </ul>
        <p><b>Variables</b></p>
        <ul>
            <li>The assignments and reads of a state machine variable highlighted in two colours; Next Highlighted Usage and Previous Highlighted Usage step through them (Ctrl+Option+Down and Ctrl+Option+Up on macOS; on Windows and Linux, assign keys under Settings | Keymap)</li>
            <li>Go to declaration, find usages, rename and completion after <code>$</code></li>
            <li>Checks for a variable that nothing assigns, one that is never read, and an assignment that AWS rejects</li>
        </ul>
        <p><b>Diagram</b></p>
        <ul>
            <li>A live diagram beside the editor that follows the caret; a click on a state or a path moves the caret there</li>
            <li>Choice paths labelled with their conditions, catch paths shown, muted or hidden, and collapsible Map and Parallel states</li>
            <li>Two layouts, zoom, and a details panel with the selected state's description, resource, variables, retriers and catchers</li>
        </ul>
        <p><b>Comments and links to code</b></p>
        <ul>
            <li>The comments of a state show as its description and notes in the details panel</li>
            <li>A file path in a comment, such as <code>lambdas/src/intake/handler.ts</code>, opens the file; <code>contracts.ts#IntakeInput</code> goes to the type's declaration, in the editor and from the details panel</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The plugin works on files named <code>*.asl.yaml</code>, <code>*.asl.yml</code> or <code>*.asl.json</code>; more patterns can be added under Settings | Languages &amp; Frameworks | Amazon States Language. It makes no network requests.</p>
        <p>Documentation: <a href="https://github.com/saigyo/aslan#readme">README</a>. Questions and problems: <a href="https://github.com/saigyo/aslan/issues">issue tracker</a>.</p>
        <p>"Amazon Web Services", "AWS" and "AWS Step Functions" are trademarks of Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. "JetBrains", "IntelliJ IDEA" and the names of other JetBrains products are trademarks of JetBrains. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Amazon or JetBrains.</p>
    ]]></description>

    <change-notes><![CDATA[
        <p>1.0.0: First release on the JetBrains Marketplace.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Editing: completion, checks, quick documentation, navigation and rename for states, and a structure view</li>
            <li>JSONata: highlighting, syntax checks, inspections, completion, documentation and local variables</li>
            <li>Variables: usage highlighting, stepping through usages, go to declaration, find usages, rename, completion and inspections</li>
            <li>Diagram: a live diagram beside the editor, with shared selection, two layouts, a catch switch and a details panel</li>
            <li>Comments: a state's description and notes in the details panel, and file paths in comments that open the code they name</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The previews for testing, 0.9.0 to 0.9.3, are on the <a href="https://github.com/saigyo/aslan/releases">releases page</a>.</p>
    ]]></change-notes>

